+The CM108B playback stream has 16 valid PCM bits but uses 32 BCLK ticks per
+channel slot (64 BCLK per stereo frame). I2S1 RX is therefore configured as:
+
+- role: slave
+- Philips I2S
+- data bit width: 16 bit
+- slot bit width: 32 bit
+- WS width: 32 BCLK
+- stereo
+
+ESP-IDF returns signed 16-bit samples. The dedicated `cm108b_rx` task promotes
+those samples to the common signed 32-bit mixer domain before writing complete
+5 ms blocks to a small bounded FIFO.
+
+## Independent clock domains
+
+The CM108B clock does NOT pace the central mixer. A dedicated RX task blocks on
+the external CM108B clock and fills a small FIFO. The mixer is paced by the
+48 kHz TAS5805M TX channel. This keeps HFP operational even if Android/CM108B
+stops sending audio clocks.
+
+The code also measures the real CM108B input rate. Expect a log such as:
+
+    AUDIO_MIXER: CM108B measured input rate: 48000.x Hz (48 kHz, ... blocks)
+
+or:
+
+    AUDIO_MIXER: CM108B measured input rate: 44100.x Hz (44.1 kHz, ... blocks)
+
+If 44.1 kHz is detected while the output is 48 kHz, an asynchronous
+44.1 -> 48 kHz rate conversion is required; increasing FIFO depth is not a
+correct fix for that clock-rate mismatch.
 
